% B1 fixture (fuzz seed 100207, delta-minimized): the representative class of
% the 31 trail-only `c-sem` observations. UNSAT; verdict correct.
%
% At the last configuration the CURRENT frame is COVERLESS (slot v0's domain is
% empty after the root assertion x0!=0). A multi-literal database clause
%   [x2<=-1 | x2>0 | x1<=-1 | x1>0 | x0<=-2 | x0>-1]
% is therefore vacuously UNIT in the frame (every non-pivot is domain-impossible
% because an empty domain falsifies every literal), with pivot x2>0. The
% trail-only semantic check (c-sem) flags the non-pivot x0>-1: no single earlier
% trail entry implies its negation x0<=-1.
%
% B1 classification (harness `cSemClass` / `nextPruningEvent` liveness gate,
% LeanFzn/Solver/Propagation/Pruning.lean:76-82): coverless=1, notSelected=0,
% selected=0. A coverless frame has no represented solution, and
% `nextPruningEvent` gates EVERY `.implied` event on `frameLiveB`, so no
% database unit is dispatched and no reason is recorded at this configuration;
% the observation is a harmless tracker limitation (the check's precondition
% is broader than the dispatch's). The domain-based falsification the
% dispatcher actually uses (`clauseRemaining`/`literalImpossible`) holds for
% every flagged non-pivot by construction.
%
% Run: .lake/build/bin/tests_lcg_harness --only --no-chrono
%        Tests/Fixtures/Solver/cex_csem_coverless_unit.fzn
% Expected: c=(2, 1) and the B1 line "coverless=1 notSelected=0 selected=0".
var -1..0: v0;
var -1..0: v1;
var 0..2: v2;
constraint all_different([v2, v1, v0]);
constraint int_times(v0, v2, v1);
constraint int_ne(v1, v2);
constraint int_min(v1, v2, v0);
solve satisfy;
